Carafe bench: OpenGL declares typeless storage images of non-integer formats as float images.
The GLSL backend declared every storage image as uimage, so stores to an RGBA8 UNORM image did nothing on
Mesa. Typeless images of float formats are now image* and their texels are bit-cast like the SPIR-V backend does.

